Usage: nfa [FILE ...]

Options:
    help                    Print this help text and exit
    reg REGEX               Creates an automaton based on the regular expression.
                            Constraints: alphabet contains integers and
                            lowercase latin letters; for Kleene star is * used,
                            parentheses are allowed, + is used for alternatives
                            and / is used for empty string.
    save ID FILE            Save the automaton in the file
    open FILE [FILE ...]    Load the listed automatons
    close ID [ID ...]       Remove automatons from memory
    close *                 Remove all automatons from memory
    list                    Lists all automatons in memory
    print ID                Prints all transitions of said automaton in table form
    empty ID                Checks if the automaton's language is empty
    deterministic ID        Checks if the automaton is deterministic
    recognize ID WORD       Returns true if the automaton recognizes the word.
                            Use / for the empty word.
    concat ID ID [ID ...]   Creates new automaton that is concatenation of all
                            listed automatons. Order is important.
    union ID ID [ID ...]    Creates a new automaton that is the union of all
                            listed automatons
    un ID                   Creates an automaton that is positive closure
                            of said automaton
    finite ID               Checks if the automaton's language is finite
    determinize ID          Creates a deterministic automaton equivalent to ID
    exit                    Exits the program
